From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:43:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Engine: collect the J714s camera setfiles and light-sensor
 calibration

A J714s install collected no IMX958 setfile and no ALS calibration the
engine's own way: the Neo's collectors run only for j700ap, and upstream's
ISP collector reads only appleh13camerad.

- omarchy_asahi.py: _j714s_peripheral_collectors, entered with the Neo's in
  the stub's collect_firmware, for device_class "j714sap" only:
  - ISP: omarchy_isp.collection_class(asahi_firmware.isp), which scans
    appleh13camerad and appleh16camerad and knows IMX958 2224_01XX and
    2226_02XX, so apple/isp_2226_02XX.dat (and 2224_01XX when present)
    reach the vendor firmware. A collection error or a missing 2226_02XX is
    logged and the install goes on (the image's first-boot
    aurora-j714s-camera-setfile is the fallback).
  - ALS: this Mac's `ioreg -r -a -n als -l` CalibrationData, first child
    chain, stored verbatim as apple/aop-als-cal.bin (then upstream's raw
    HmCA factory copy). A failure is logged, never fatal, and no other
    Mac's data is substituted.
  - The fallback archive keeps appleh16camerad, as the Neo's does
    (_WithNeoFirmwareArchive without the Neo's raw LSCI).
- omarchy_als.py: j714s_calibration / read_j714s_calibration, gathered
  from aurora-silicon/aurora-installer asahi_firmware/als.py (MIT), as
  tools/als-calibration/save-als-cal.py does.
- Tests: J714sPeripheralCollectionTests (both collectors and the archive on
  the J714s, failures logged not fatal, the Neo and other boards
  untouched), J714sAlsTests; the Centauri flow test checks the stub enters
  the J714s collectors.
- Engine renamed v0.9.2-omarchy.20261113.774d9abc59d3 and repacked from
  the authenticated engine.28 base: 17913790 bytes, sha256
  927bf3f3a22a3549c807f7526c4e9cfe0626ad716d49e731ae5bac2dd97cfd42, two
  identical repacks.

Checked: engine overlay tests (441), engine tooling tests, test/all,
image-builder/test/all (except the edge-dispatch template test that
already fails on release 1), engine_pin.py check, verify-source-lock.py,
read-validation-engine.py, prepare-engine.py. Not run on a J714s: the
ioreg layout and appleh16camerad contents are as save-als-cal.py and the
J714c setfile work found them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
